#23822
At the Edge of a Pond~
   A creek flows into a pond here.  The creek, too large to jump across, flows
in from the northwest.  This is the northwest shore of the roughly circular
pond.  The pond looks too deep to wade through.  Trees and shrubs line the
shoreline of the pond, effectively blocking it in on three sides.  This
shoreline continues south of here.    
~
